# Copy to .env.local (git-ignored) and fill in. Only VITE_* values reach the browser,
# so NEVER put secrets (API keys, payment keys, service-role keys) in any VITE_ variable.

# Public contact email used by the "Get in touch" button, the contact page and the request "Open in email app" action.
# Leave empty to use the built-in default (the owner's address, see src/config/site.ts). Set it to your branded address
# (for example hello@yourdomain.com) when you have one. Set it to "none" to switch email contact off.
VITE_CONTACT_EMAIL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase (Stage 1: the client is prepared, but no page uses it yet)
#
# Only these TWO values belong in this project, and only in your own git-ignored .env.local.
# Both are PUBLIC by design: they are shipped to every visitor's browser. Customer data is
# protected by Row Level Security inside the database, not by hiding these values.
#
# Find them in the Supabase dashboard: Project Settings -> API
#   Project URL      e.g. https://abcdefghijklmnop.supabase.co   (local test stack: http://127.0.0.1:54321)
#   Publishable key  starts with sb_publishable_   (the legacy "anon" key also works; both are public)
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
#
# Customer sign-up and log-in are OFF unless this is exactly "true". Keep it empty until the database has been
# installed and checked (adding the two values above is not enough on its own, on purpose).
VITE_ACCOUNTS_ENABLED=
#
# NEVER put any of the following in this project - not in this file, not in any VITE_ variable,
# not in source code, not in commits, and never paste them into a chat:
#   - the secret key (sb_secret_...) or the service-role key
#   - the database password or any postgres:// connection string
#   - the JWT secret
# The app refuses to start its Supabase client if it is given a secret/service-role key.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Booking and payments (server only: no VITE_ prefix, so none of these reach the browser)
#
# On this computer, with these left empty, booking still works end to end: payments are simulated on a
# test page and bookings are kept in .data/ (git-ignored). Add a Dodo TEST key to use Dodo's real
# test checkout instead (no real money moves).
#   1. Dodo dashboard (Test mode) -> Developer -> API keys -> create a key, paste it below.
#   2. Run: npm run dodo:setup   (creates the "Ankiro consultation" product and fills in DODO_PRODUCT_ID)
DODO_PAYMENTS_API_KEY=
DODO_PAYMENTS_ENVIRONMENT=test_mode
DODO_PRODUCT_ID=
# Price (in rupees) used in test mode for consultations that have no real price yet. Default and minimum 50,
# because Dodo refuses payments under US$0.50.
BOOKING_TEST_PRICE_INR=
#
# On the live site these are set in Vercel -> Project -> Settings -> Environment Variables, never here:
#   DODO_PAYMENTS_API_KEY (live key), DODO_PAYMENTS_ENVIRONMENT=live_mode, DODO_PRODUCT_ID (live product),
#   DODO_PAYMENTS_WEBHOOK_KEY (from the webhook you add in Dodo for https://ankiro.in/api/dodo-webhook),
#   SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY (Supabase -> Project Settings -> API keys -> secret key), SITE_URL=https://ankiro.in
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
